        <skos:definition rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Near infrared transmission spectroscopy is a type of vibrational spectroscopy where the transmission of near infrared radiation (0.8-2 µm) through a sample is detected. [CHMO]</skos:definition>
