        <skos:definition rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">In mathematics, tensors are geometric objects that describe linear relations between geometric vectors, scalars, and other tensors. Elementary examples of such relations include the dot product, the cross product, and linear maps. The tensor datum is a facet that uses a tensor as an abstract mathematical description. [Wikipedia]</skos:definition>
