        <skos:altLabel rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">vector value</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:definition rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">In mathematics, physics, and engineering, a Euclidean vector (sometimes called a geometric or spatial vector, or—as here—simply a vector) is a geometric object that has magnitude (or length) and direction. [Wikipedia]</skos:definition>
