        <skos:definition rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Signal-to-noise ratio (USP621) is a signal-to-noise ratio (peak-to-peak) where the noise is calculated over a period that is a minimum of 5 times the peak width. [Allotrope]</skos:definition>
        <skos:prefLabel rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">signal-to-noise ratio (USP621)</skos:prefLabel>
    </owl:Class>
    


