        <skos:definition rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Signal-to-noise ratio (EP2.2.46) is a signal-to-noise ratio (peak-to-peak) where the noise is calculated over a period that is a minimum of 20 times the peak width. [Allotrope]</skos:definition>
        <skos:prefLabel rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">signal-to-noise ratio (EP2.2.46)</skos:prefLabel>
    </owl:Class>
    


