        <skos:definition rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">A half height multiplier signal to noise setting (USP) is a data processing setting that indicates the half height multiplier that is to be used in determining the baseline region for calculating noise in USP S/N calculations. [Allotrope]</skos:definition>
