        <skos:definition rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">A maximum allowable noise setting is a data processing setting that indicates the maximum allowed noise value for measured noise in order for a run to be deemed valid. [Allotrope]</skos:definition>
