        <obo:IAO_0000115 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">The simplest carboxylic acid, containing a single carbon. Occurs naturally in various sources including the venom of bee and ant stings, and is a useful organic synthetic reagent. Principally used as a preservative and antibacterial agent in livestock feed. Induces severe metabolic acidosis and ocular injury in human subjects.</obo:IAO_0000115>
