        <obo:IAO_0000115 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Quarks comprise one of two classes of the fundamental particles. Quarks possess fractional electric charges and are not observed in free state. The word &quot;quark&quot; first appears in James Joyce&apos;s Finnegans Wake and has been chosen by Murray Gell-Mann as a name for fundamental building blocks of particles.</obo:IAO_0000115>
